      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "> Not sure if fair, as the model will know what to do depending on the puzzle id. So it appears as not being generic (on the case of ARC) but biased/specialized on each task. The trained model may not work properly if we do not inform the task id later, and may fail on completely new/unseen tasks\n\nIndeed, I believe this is a severe problem, it's not in-context learning. I believe those frontier model (Gemini, GPT) is definitely not using this strategy. ",
